  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1224 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nWe are going to see quiet weather throughout the week as the upper\nlevel ridge takes hold over the region. Highs will warm to near \nrecord territory Tuesday through Thursday. The apex of the ridge \nwill be over us during the middle of the week and that will be the\npeak heating, Wednesday will the day greatest at risk for \nbreaking records with some areas reaching the lower 90s. Late week\nand into the weekend an upper level trough will dig into the \nGreat Lakes. This will break the ridge down and bring falling \nheights and push a cold front through Middle TN. Highs will start \nto cool on Friday with them falling into the mid 70s to lower 80s.\nThe colder air will really filter in Saturday with highs dropping\ninto the 60s! Rain chances throughout the week are near zero and \nthe front late week looks to be a dry front.",
